            <profile id="f7ea-d17f-4667-6434" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, heavy armour and shield. May ride a warhorse (+16 pts). May have a thrusting spear (+2 pts), partial plate armour (+2 pts) and cloth barding (+4 pts). If on foot, may have a two-handed weapon (+2 pts). May take either the Kniaz or the Voyvoda as the Army General. Stubborn if on foot. In Eastern Russian armies a Kniaz may be upgraded to Veliki Kniaz (+15 pts, WS6, I6); a Veliki Kniaz may only lead a unit of Senior Druzhniks. (Armies of Chivalry p.48)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="4983-9bb9-f76c-4811" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">4+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
