  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="105c-3cff-b7ca-a619" name="Medieval Russian States (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF THE MEDIEVAL RUSSIAN STATES 1276-1501 (Armies of Chivalry, pp.48-49). Shieldwall: units that benefit from the Shieldwall special rule may form a Shieldwall instead of moving, causing all enemy attacks from the front to suffer -1 to hit (shooting and hand-to-hand), lasting until the unit moves or is defeated in hand-to-hand combat. Superior Shock Cavalry and Eastern Shock Cavalry as given in the army rules.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Medieval Russian States - Eastern Russian States]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 33%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Vassals, Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 33%
  Muscovy, Vladimir, Suzdal, Ryazan, Tver. Characters up to 25%, Cavalry at least 33%, Infantry up to 50%, Vassals, Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to 33% (includes 0-1 light cannon for every 1,500 pts). Handgunners and Artillery should be taken only after 1425. If Allies from the Western Russian States are taken, no Tartar Nobles or Tartar Warriors may be taken. Allies (documented only): Western Russian States - 0-1 Boyar (acts as General for the Western contingent), Junior Druzhniks, Dismounted Druzhniks, Horse Archers and all Urban Militia units.
[Medieval Russian States - Western Russian States]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Vassals, Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Novgorod, Pskov, Galych. Characters up to 25%, Cavalry up to 50%, Infantry at least 33%, Vassals, Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to 25% (includes 0-1 light cannon for every 1,000 pts). Handgunners and Artillery should be taken only after 1380. Allies (documented only): Eastern Russian States - 0-1 Boyar (acts as General for the Eastern contingent), Junior Druzhniks, Horse Archers, all Urban Militia units and Tartar Warriors.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
